ol\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(p[\\\"repo\\\"], \\\"../wai\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(p[\\\"decision\\\"], \\\"dry_run\\\");\\n    assert_eq!(p[\\\"reason\\\"], serde_json::Value::Null);\\n    assert_eq!(p[\\\"bd_issue_id\\\"], serde_json::Value::Null);\\n}\\n\\nfn three_models() -> Vec<String> {\"}]}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":12760,"output":1725,"cacheRead":49280,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1113,"totalTokens":63765,"cost":{"input":0.001914,"output":0.0008625,"cacheRead":0.0014784,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0042549}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"All clear. Plan confirmed. Now begin the RED phase for step 1. Write the failing test in tests/routing.rs.\n\nTest 1:\n\n```rust\n// ── doc-coverage fault intake (evallerina-e4x) ─────────────────────────────\n\n/// A doc-audit report row (src/doc_audit.rs report_row shape): one\n/// failing check per audit row, carrying the check-code. Bridged rows\n/// additionally carry `kind` and `model` attribution (the battery-wide\n/// scope of a static audit).\nfn doc_audit_row(tool: &str, model: &str, code: &str) -> serde_json::Value {\n    json!({\n        \"kind\": \"doc_audit\",\n        \"report_version\": 1,\n        \"scenario\": \"doc-audit\",\n        \"tool\": tool,\n        \"model\": model,\n        \"status\": \"failed\",\n        \"checks\": [{\"name\": \"doc:sample-feature\", \"passed\": false, \"code\": code}]\n    })\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn undocumented_feature_audit_row_crosses_threshold_to_dry_run_proposal() {\n    let rows: Vec<serde_json::Value> = [\"m/a\", \"m/b\", \"m/c\"]\n        .iter()\n        .map(|m| doc_audit_row(\"wai\", m, \"ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\"))\n        .collect();\n    let proposals = routing::propose(&rows, &three_models(), &recorded_wai, &repo_map())\n        .expect(\"doc-audit rows route like any other fault row\");\n    assert_eq!(proposals.len(), 1);\n    let p = &proposals[0].to_json();\n    assert_eq!(p[\"scenario\"], \"doc-audit\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"fault_class\"], \"ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"token\"], \"evallerina:doc-audit:ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"tool\"], \"wai\", \"repo keyed on the audited tool\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"repo\"], \"../wai\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"decision\"], \"dry_run\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"bd_issue_id\"], serde_json::Value::Null);\n}\n```\n\nWait — repo_map() helper maps \"wai\" → \"../wai\". With RoutingEntry change later, repo_map() helper needs updating — but that happens at step 3. At step 1, propose still takes BTreeMap<String,String>. OK.\n\nBut note: at step 1, recorded_wai(\"doc-audit\") returns None → loud error! The doc branch must bypass scenario_tool_of. So implementation must move resolution lazily. In step 1 implementation: move scenario_tool_of call into the tool-fault (None) branch, and add doc branch keyed on row_tool.\n\nAlso threshold: 3 models → crosses. But note the current code filters by tally.models.len() — bridged rows have model field → 3 distinct. Good.\n\nNow implement step 1. The current match:\n\n```rust\nmatch check.get(\"code\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str) {\n    Some(code) if code.starts_with(\"ERR_\") => continue,\n    _ => { tool_fault using recorded_tool }\n}\n```\n\nChange to:\n\n```rust\nmatch check.get(\"code\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str) {\n    // Doc-coverage faults (evallerina-fok/e4x): the two audit codes\n    // route like any other fault — the audited tool (the row's `tool`\n    // field; doc-audit rows carry it authoritatively) is the repo key,\n    // and the fault class is the check code itself.\n    Some(code) if code == crate::doc_audit::ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED => { tally with fault_class code, tool row_tool }\n    // Agent faults are never routed ...\n    Some(_) => continue,\n    // Tool fault ...\n    _ => { resolve recorded_tool lazily here }\n}\n```\n\nSince recorded_tool resolution moves into the None branch, restructure: remove the pre-loop `let recorded_tool = ...` and inside None arm:\n\n```rust\n_ => {\n    let recorded_tool = scenario_tool_of(scenario).ok_or_else(...)?;\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nCareful with borrow: scenario is &str from row; fine.\n\nAlso doc codes referenced via crate::doc_audit constants — good, single source.\n\nLet me now wri