d_upstream\"));\n    assert!(spy.create_calls().is_empty(), \"upstream tools are NEVER filed\");\n}\n```\n\nBut existing tests use repo_map() returning BTreeMap<String,String> and pass to propose — those will break compilation when signature changes. So the implementation step must update repo_map() helper and all propose/file usages in tests. Also report.rs attach_routing + run_routing_step + tests/report_aggregation.rs. And remove/replace routing::parse_routing_toml — used in report.rs; tests routing_toml_parses_tools_to_repos, routing_toml_missing_repo_is_loud pin it. Options: keep parse_routing_toml but return BTreeMap<String, RoutingEntry> (delegate to routing_parity::parse_routing_entries). Its two tests keep passing shape-wise? routing_toml_parses_tools_to_repos asserts map.get(\"wai\").map(String::as_str) == Some(\"../wai\") — would break with RoutingEntry values. Update those tests to assert .repo. Cleanest: delete routing::parse_routing_toml entirely, use routing_parity::parse_routing_entries everywhere, move its two tests to target parse_routing_entries (or rely on existing parity tests). Let me check tests/routing_parity.rs already covers parse_routing_entries... grep."}}
