{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":5942,"output":4291,"cacheRead":71680,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2610,"totalTokens":81913,"cost":{"input":0.0008912999999999999,"output":0.0021455,"cacheRead":0.0021504,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0051871999999999995}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Step 5: bridge function in doc_audit.rs + CLI wiring + hermetic CLI tests (dry-run default anti-goal).\n\nRED first: write the hermetic CLI test that runs `evallerina doc-audit` in a sandbox git repo with a fixture binary + doc surfaces + doc_audit.toml + routing.toml, asserting:\n1. Output JSON has \"proposals\" array with decision dry_run (mapped tool) — RED (no proposals field yet).\n2. Dry-run default: no --file → no bd anywhere (assert no .beads created; also assert decisions ∈ {dry_run, skipped}).\n3. --file in a non-beads mapped repo → skipped/bd_failure, exit 0 (proves --file is the only escalation, and failures aren't fatal).\n\nSandbox setup:\n- git init sandbox (discover_root uses git rev-parse --show-toplevel in cwd).\n- doc_audit.toml: [fixtool] repo = \".\" binary = \"fixtool\"\n- routing.toml: [fixtool] repo = \".\" (mapped, relative → resolves to root)\n- fixtool: executable shell script printing --help with --some-flag → surface token \"someflag\".\n- README.md WITHOUT \"some flag\" → ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED for token someflag.\n- registry: ordered_ids — 4 models, threshold 3 → bridged rows cross.\n\nCLI: `bin().args([\"doc-audit\"]).current_dir(&sb)`.\n\nOutput: pretty JSON on stdout. Parse, find audit_rows includes someflag/ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED; proposals: one row token \"evallerina:doc-audit:ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\", tool fixtool, decision dry_run.\n\nWait — decision: repo \".\" resolves via resolve_repo? propose returns repo string as-is from the map (\".\" — relative). main.rs will just pass repo_map.get → repo \".\". Fine — Some(\".\").\n\n--file test: `doc-audit --file` → file_proposals(true) in cwd \".\" → bd search/list fail (not a beads repo) → create fails → skipped/bd_failure. Exit 0. Also assert no .beads dir created... bd create in non-beads dir — bd might create .beads? bd init creates; create fails presumably without init. Existing test bd_failure_in_target_repo_is_skipped_never_fatal does exactly this in a fresh dir. OK.\n\nAlso the dry-run-default anti-goal: assert that running WITHOUT --file leaves no .beads and proposals decisions are dry_run. Also assert the proposals JSONL writing flag... For smoke I need proposals JSONL written to research/. Add `--proposals-out <path>`: writes routing::to_jsonl(&proposals). Test: --proposals-out writes file with one line.\n\nWhere to put the CLI tests? New file tests/doc_audit_cli.rs.\n\nNow implementation:\n\n1. doc_audit.rs bridge:\n\n```rust\n/// Bridge doc-audit report rows into the fault-routing intake\n/// (evallerina-e4x, openspec add-ecosystem-doc-evals task 3.2). A\n/// tier-0 audit is a static, model-independent check: its findings\n/// apply to the whole configured battery by construction, so each\n/// report row is attributed to every configured model id. This keeps\n/// routing's cross-model threshold semantics verbatim (design D3 — no\n/// new routing semantics): the battery-wide finding crosses the\n/// battery-wide threshold honestly, with provenance naming every\n/// attributed model.\npub fn routing_rows(\n    report_rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    models: &[String],\n) -> Vec<serde_json::Value> {\n    report_rows\n        .iter()\n        .flat_map(|row| {\n            models.iter().map(move |model| {\n                let mut routed = row.clone();\n                routed[\"kind\"] = serde_json::json!(\"doc_audit\");\n                routed[\"model\"] = serde_json::json!(model);\n                routed\n            })\n        })\n        .collect()\n}\n```\n\n2. main.rs DocAudit variant:\n\n```rust\nDocAudit {\n    /// Write the dry-run routing proposals (proposed-tickets.jsonl\n    /// content, one JSON object per line) to this path.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    proposals_out: Option<String>,\n    /// File the routed proposals in their mapped repositories\n    /// (explicit cross-repo write authorization, Phase 2). Dry-run is\n    /// the default: without --file no bd call ever happens.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    file: bool,\n},\n```\n\nHandler run_doc_audit(proposals_out, file): after report_rows computed:\n\n```rust\n// Routing intake (evallerina-e4x): doc-audit rows feed the existing\n// fault-routing path. Dry-run by default; --file is the only\n// escalation (anti-goal: no filing without explicit authorization).\nlet configured: Vec<String> = ordered_ids().into_iter().map(String::from).collect();\nlet intake = evallerina::doc_audit::routing_rows(&report_rows, &configured);\nlet routing_toml_path = root_path.join(\"routing.toml\");\nlet routing_toml = std::fs::read_to_string(&routing_toml_path)\n    .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot read {}: {e}\", routing_toml_path.display()))?;\nlet repo_map = evallerina::routing_parity::parse_routing_entries(&routing_toml)?;\nlet no_recorded_tool = |_: &str| None;\nlet mut proposals = evallerina::routing::propose(&intake, &configured, &no_recorded_tool, &repo_map)?;\nlet mut runner = evallerina::routing::run_bd;\nevallerina::routing::file_proposals(&mut proposals, file, &mut runner)?;\nif let Some(out) = &proposals_out {\n    std::fs::write(out, evallerina::routing::to_jsonl(&proposals))\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot write proposals to {out}: {e}\"))?;\n}\n```\n\nAnd add \"proposals\" to output JSON: proposals array of to_json.\n\nWait — scenario_tool_of closure type: propose takes &dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<String>. `|_: &str| None` needs type annotation: `let no_recorded_tool = |_: &str| -> Option<String> { None };` then `&no_recorded_tool`.\n\nHmm — wait, is it right for doc-audit to ALWAYS run routing? tier0 runs doc-audit > /dev/null; routing.toml is checked in → fine. propose errors loudly if registry empty — registry is const. OK.\n\nAlso update Command::DocAudit match arm: `Command::DocAudit { proposals_out, file } => match run_doc_audit(proposals_out.as_deref(), file)`.\n\n3. Also update main.rs doc comment for DocAudit subcommand and run_doc_audit doc comment.\n\nTest file tests/doc_audit_cli.rs:\n\n```rust\nfn bin() -> Command { Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\")) }\n\nfn sandbox(tag) -> PathBuf {...}\n\nfn seed_doc_audit_sandbox(tag: &str) -> PathBuf {\n    let dir = sandbox(tag);\n    // git init so discover_root resolves to the sandbox\n    run git init -q\n    // fixture binary on PATH\n    write fixtool script: #!/bin/sh\\necho \"Usage: fixtool [OPTIONS]\"... need a long flag: echo \"  --some-flag    do the thing\"\n    chmod +x\n    // README without the token → ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\n    write README.md: \"# fixtool\\n\\nRuns the thing.\\n\"\n    // configs\n    doc_audit.toml: [fixtool]\\nrepo = \".\"\\nbinary = \"fixtool\"\\n\n    routing.toml: [fixtool]\\nrepo = \".\"\\n\n    dir\n}\n```\n\nWait — repo = \".\" for doc_audit config: main.rs resolves repo relative to root and checks is_dir → \".\" is dir → scan inventory. Good. routing.toml repo \".\" → proposal repo \".\".\n\nHmm — one wrinkle: harvest_doc_tokens from README: \"Runs the thing.\" tokens: runs, the, thing. Surface tokens: help? extract_surface harvests: --help output of fixtool: \"Usage: fixtool\" ... \"--some-flag\". Tokens: someflag. Also maybe \"usage\", \"fixtool\"? harvest_tokens only picks long flags, subcommands under \"Commands:\" header, exit codes. \"Usage:\" line has no --flag. So surface = {someflag}. README lacks someflag → ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED. \n\nBut wait — script's --help output: I write the script so `fixtool --help` prints usage. extract_surface runs `fixtool --help` — my script ignores args, prints usage. Good.\n\nPATH env: .env(\"PATH\", dir path) — replaces PATH entirely; scripts run via Command::new(\"fixtool\") need /bin/sh — shebang works. Use #!/bin/sh. Fine on this system.\n\nAssertions test 1 (dry_run default + proposals in output + jsonl):\n\n```rust\n#[test]\nfn doc_audit_routes_dry_run_by_default_and_never_files() {\n    let sb = seed(\"dry-run-default\");\n    let out_path = sb.join(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\");\n    let out = bin().args([\"doc-audit\", \"--proposals-out\", out_path...]).current_dir(&sb).output()...\n    assert success\n    let v: Value = serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout)\n    // the audit found the undocumented feature\n    assert audit_rows contains {\"tool\":\"fixtool\",\"token\":\"someflag\",\"code\":\"ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\"}\n    // routing proposals are dry_run, keyed on the audited tool\n    let proposals = v[\"proposals\"].as_array().unwrap();\n    assert_eq!(len, 1)\n    p[\"decision\"]==\"dry_run\"; p[\"token\"]==\"evallerina:doc-audit:ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\"; p[\"tool\"]==\"fixtool\"\n    // dry-run default: no bd anywhere — no .beads, and the JSONL exists with the same row\n    assert!(!sb.join(\".beads\").exists());\n    let jsonl = read out_path; one line; parse token.\n}\n```\n\nWait — will proposals len be 1? Audit rows: 1 row (someflag, ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED). Bridged: 4 models. propose: fault key (doc-audit, ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED, fixtool) → threshold min(3, 4)=3, distinct models 4 → crosses → 1 proposal. But careful: audit might find MORE tokens undocumented (e.g. \"help\"? harvest_tokens: does \"Usage: fixtool [OPTIONS]\" produce... no flags besides --some-flag. But stderr also parsed; script prints only stdout. OK 1 token. But also \"exit...\" none. Good.\n\nActually wait — README tokens: harvest_doc_tokens(\"Runs the thing.\") → runs, the, thing... \"the\" piece etc. None equal someflag. Fine.\n\nTest 2 (--file escalation in non-beads repo → skipped/bd_failure, exit 0):\n\n```rust\n#[test]\nfn doc_audit_file_flag_is_the_only_escalation_and_bd_failure_is_not_fatal() {\n    let sb = seed(\"file-escalation\");\n    let out = bin().args([\"doc-audit\", \"--file\"]).current_dir(&sb).output();\n    assert success (exit 0)\n    v[\"proposals\"][0][\"decision\"] == \"skipped\", reason \"bd_failure\"\n}\n```\n\nHmm wait — will bd create actually fail in the sandbox? bd without init... the existing routing test bd_failure_in_target_repo_is_skipped_never_fatal uses Sandbox::fresh (no bd init) and asserts skipped/bd_failure — so yes bd create fails there. But careful: bd might behave differently based on HOME/config? Existing test proves the behavior. But also `bd search` in a non-beads dir — fine.\n\nAlso: bd might be slow-ish; two bd calls. Acceptable.\n\nAlso assert in test 1 that stdout decisions only dry_run/skipped (dry-run default anti-goal): trivially by the single dry_run row.\n\nNow write the CLI tests (RED — they'll fail on missing --proposals-out flag and missing proposals field), then implement."}}
