{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":5942,"output":4291,"cacheRead":71680,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":2610,"totalTokens":81913,"cost":{"input":0.0008912999999999999,"output":0.0021455,"cacheRead":0.0021504,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0051871999999999995}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-6757b7fe-d890-4dc6-a39b-4a9f0d48f341","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"tests/doc_audit_cli.rs","content":"//! Purpose: end-to-end CLI contract tests for `evallerina doc-audit`\n//! routing intake (evallerina-e4x, openspec add-ecosystem-doc-evals\n//! tasks 3.1–3.2).\n//! Responsibilities: pin the dry-run default through the binary — the\n//! doc-audit routing step emits proposal rows and never files without\n//! explicit `--file` — plus the `--proposals-out` JSONL artifact and\n//! the non-fatal bd-failure path under `--file`.\n//! Rationale: the filing path can create real tickets in real repos;\n//! its anti-goals (no filing without `--file`, dry-run default) must\n//! hold end to end through the binary, not just through the library\n//! API. Every test runs in an isolated git sandbox with a fixture\n//! binary — the trackers of evallerina and every family repo are\n//! never touched.\n\nuse serde_json::Value;\nuse std::process::Command;\n\nfn bin() -> Command {\n    Command::new(env!(\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_evallerina\"))\n}\n\n/// Seed a hermetic doc-audit sandbox: a git repo (so `doc-audit`'s\n/// worktree-safe root discovery resolves here) containing a fixture\n/// binary whose `--help` exposes `--some-flag`, a README that never\n/// mentions it (→ `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`), and the two checked-in\n/// config shapes mapping the tool to this same sandbox repo.\nfn seed_sandbox(tag: &str) -> std::path::PathBuf {\n    let dir = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!(\n        \"evallerina-doc-audit-cli-{tag}-{}-{}\",\n        std::process::id(),\n        std::time::SystemTime::now()\n            .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)\n            .expect(\"clock\")\n            .as_nanos(),\n    ));\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).expect(\"create sandbox\");\n    let git = Command::new(\"git\")\n        .args([\"init\", \"-q\"])\n        .current_dir(&dir)\n        .output()\n        .expect(\"git init in sandbox\");\n    assert!(git.status.success(), \"git init failed in sandbox\");\n\n    // Fixture binary: `--help` harvests exactly one feature token.\n    let fixtool = dir.join(\"fixtool\");\n    std::fs::write(\n        &fixtool,\n        \"#!/bin/sh\\necho \\\"Usage: fixtool [OPTIONS]\\\"\\necho \\\"  --some-flag  do the thing\\\"\\n\",\n    )\n    .expect(\"write fixtool\");\n    #[cfg(unix)]\n    {\n        use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\n        std::fs::set_permissions(&fixtool, std::fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755))\n            .expect(\"chmod fixtool\");\n    }\n\n    // Docs never document the flag → the audit row exists.\n    std::fs::write(dir.join(\"README.md\"), \"# fixtool\\n\\nRuns the thing.\\n\")\n        .expect(\"write README\");\n\n    std::fs::write(\n        dir.join(\"doc_audit.toml\"),\n        \"[fixtool]\\nrepo = \\\".\\\"\\nbinary = \\\"fixtool\\\"\\n\",\n    )\n    .expect(\"write doc_audit.toml\");\n    std::fs::write(dir.join(\"routing.toml\"), \"[fixtool]\\nrepo = \\\".\\\"\\n\")\n        .expect(\"write routing.toml\");\n    dir\n}\n\n/// Run `doc-audit` inside the sandbox with the fixture binary on PATH.\nfn run_doc_audit(sb: &std::path::Path, extra: &[&str]) -> (std::process::Output, Value) {\n    let out = bin()\n        .args([\"doc-audit\"])\n        .args(extra)\n        .current_dir(sb)\n        .env(\"PATH\", sb)\n        .output()\n        .expect(\"run doc-audit\");\n    let json: Value = serde_json::from_slice(&out.stdout).expect(\"doc-audit prints JSON\");\n    (out, json)\n}\n\n/// The one expected audit finding in the sandbox: `--some-flag` is\n/// undocumented, so it must appear as an audit row and route.\nfn undocumented_someflag(json: &Value) {\n    let rows = json[\"audit_rows\"].as_array().expect(\"audit_rows array\");\n    assert!(\n        rows.iter().any(|r| {\n            r[\"tool\"] == \"fixtool\"\n                && r[\"token\"] == \"someflag\"\n                && r[\"code\"] == \"ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\"\n        }),\n        \"expected the someflag ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED row, got: {rows:?}\"\n    );\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn doc_audit_routes_dry_run_by_default_and_never_files() {\n    let sb = seed_sandbox(\"dry-run-default\");\n    let jsonl_path = sb.join(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\");\n    let (out, json) = run_doc_audit(&sb, &[\"--proposals-out\", jsonl_path.to_str().unwrap()]);\n    assert!(\n        out.status.success(),\n        \"doc-audit exits zero on findings (the audit is the record): {}\",\n        String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr)\n    );\n    undocumented_someflag(&json);\n\n    // The routing intake is part of the output: one dry-run proposal\n    // keyed on the audited tool, with the fingerprint token.\n    let proposals = json[\"proposals\"].as_array().expect(\"proposals array\");\n    assert_eq!(proposals.len(), 1, \"one fault key above threshold\");\n    let p = &proposals[0];\n    assert_eq!(p[\"decision\"], \"dry_run\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"tool\"], \"fixtool\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"token\"], \"evallerina:doc-audit:ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"bd_issue_id\"], Value::Null, \"dry-run files nothing\");\n\n    // Dry-run default anti-goal: without --file no bd call ever\n    // happens — the sandbox tracker is untouched.\n    assert!(!sb.join(\".beads\").exists(), \"no filing without --file\");\n\n    // The JSONL artifact is the proposed-tickets.jsonl schema: one\n    // machine-checkable object per line.\n    let jsonl = std::fs::read_to_string(&jsonl_path).expect(\"proposals JSONL written\");\n    let lines: Vec<&str> = jsonl.lines().collect();\n    assert_eq!(lines.len(), 1, \"one object per line\");\n    let row: Value = serde_json::from_str(lines[0]).expect(\"each line is a JSON object\");\n    assert_eq!(row[\"token\"], \"evallerina:doc-audit:ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\");\n}\n\n#[test]\nfn doc_audit_file_flag_is_the_only_escalation_and_bd_failure_is_not_fatal() {\n    let sb = seed_sandbox(\"file-escalation\");\n    let (out, json) = run_doc_audit(&sb, &[\"--file\"]);\n    // Filing is an optimization over the report: a bd failure in the\n    // target repo is the record (skipped/bd_failure), never an error.\n    assert!(\n        out.status.success(),\n        \"bd failure must not crash doc-audit: {}\",\n        String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stderr)\n    );\n    let p = &json[\"proposals\"].as_array().expect(\"proposals array\")[0];\n    assert_eq!(p[\"decision\"], \"skipped\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"reason\"], \"bd_failure\");\n    assert_eq!(p[\"bd_issue_id\"], Value::Null);\n}\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Step 5: bridge function in doc_audit.rs + CLI wiring + hermetic CLI tests (dry-run default anti-goal).\n\nRED first: write the hermetic CLI test that runs `evallerina doc-audit` in a sandbox git repo with a fixture binary + doc surfaces + doc_audit.toml + routing.toml, asserting:\n1. Output JSON has \"proposals\" array with decision dry_run (mapped tool) — RED (no proposals field yet).\n2. Dry-run default: no --file → no bd anywhere (assert no .beads created; also assert decisions ∈ {dry_run, skipped}).\n3. --file in a non-beads mapped repo → skipped/bd_failure, exit 0 (proves --file is the only escalation, and failures aren't fatal).\n\nSandbox setup:\n- git init sandbox (discover_root uses git rev-parse --show-toplevel in cwd).\n- doc_audit.toml: [fixtool] repo = \".\" binary = \"fixtool\"\n- routing.toml: [fixtool] repo = \".\" (mapped, relative → resolves to root)\n- fixtool: executable shell script printing --help with --some-flag → surface token \"someflag\".\n- README.md WITHOUT \"some flag\" → ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED for token someflag.\n- registry: ordered_ids — 4 models, threshold 3 → bridged rows cross.\n\nCLI: `bin().args([\"doc-audit\"]).current_dir(&sb)`.\n\nOutput: pretty JSON on stdout. Parse, find audit_rows includes someflag/ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED; proposals: one row token \"evallerina:doc-audit:ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED\", tool fixtool, decision dry_run.\n\nWait — decision: repo \".\" resolves via resolve_repo? propose returns repo string as-is from the map (\".\" — relative). main.rs will just pass repo_map.get → repo \".\". Fine — Some(\".\").\n\n--file test: `doc-audit --file` → file_proposals(true) in cwd \".\" → bd search/list fail (not a beads repo) → create fails → skipped/bd_failure. Exit 0. Also assert no .beads dir created... bd create in non-beads dir — bd might create .beads? bd init creates; create fails presumably without init. Existing test bd_failure_in_target_repo_is_skipped_never_fatal does exactly this in a fresh dir. OK.\n\nAlso the dry-run-default anti-goal: assert that running WITHOUT --file leaves no .beads and proposals decisions are dry_run. Also assert the proposals JSONL writing flag... For smoke I need proposals JSONL written to research/. Add `--proposals-out <path>`: writes routing::to_jsonl(&proposals). Test: --proposals-out writes file with one line.\n\nWhere to put the CLI tests? New file tests/doc_audit_cli.rs.\n\nNow implementation:\n\n1. doc_audit.rs bridge:\n\n```rust\n/// Bridge doc-audit report rows into the fault-routing intake\n/// (evallerina-e4x, openspec add-ecosystem-doc-evals task 3.2). A\n/// tier-0 audit is a static, model-independent check: its findings\n/// apply to the whole configured battery by construction, so each\n/// report row is attributed to every configured model id. This keeps\n/// routing's cross-model threshold semantics verbatim (design D3 — no\n/// new routing semantics): the battery-wide finding crosses the\n/// battery-wide threshold honestly, with provenance naming every\n/// attributed model.\npub fn routing_rows(\n    report_rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    models: &[String],\n) -> Vec<serde_json::Value> {\n    report_rows\n        .iter()\n        .flat_map(|row| {\n            models.iter().map(move |model| {\n                let mut routed = row.clone();\n                routed[\"kind\"] = serde_json::json!(\"doc_audit\");\n                routed[\"model\"] = serde_json::json!(model);\n                routed\n            })\n        })\n        .collect()\n}\n```\n\n2. main.rs DocAudit variant:\n\n```rust\nDocAudit {\n    /// Write the dry-run routing proposals (proposed-tickets.jsonl\n    /// content, one JSON object per line) to this path.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    proposals_out: Option<String>,\n    /// File the routed proposals in their mapped repositories\n    /// (explicit cross-repo write authorization, Phase 2). Dry-run is\n    /// the default: without --file no bd call ever happens.\n    #[arg(long)]\n    file: bool,\n},\n```\n\nHandler run_doc_audit(proposals_out, file): after report_rows computed:\n\n```rust\n// Routing intake (evallerina-e4x): doc-audit rows feed the existing\n// fault-routing path. Dry-run by default; --file is the only\n// escalation (anti-goal: no filing without explicit authorization).\nlet configured: Vec<String> = ordered_ids().into_iter().map(String::from).collect();\nlet intake = evallerina::doc_audit::routing_rows(&report_rows, &configured);\nlet routing_toml_path = root_path.join(\"routing.toml\");\nlet routing_toml = std::fs::read_to_string(&routing_toml_path)\n    .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot read {}: {e}\", routing_toml_path.display()))?;\nlet repo_map = evallerina::routing_parity::parse_routing_entries(&routing_toml)?;\nlet no_recorded_tool = |_: &str| None;\nlet mut proposals = evallerina::routing::propose(&intake, &configured, &no_recorded_tool, &repo_map)?;\nlet mut runner = evallerina::routing::run_bd;\nevallerina::routing::file_proposals(&mut proposals, file, &mut runner)?;\nif let Some(out) = &proposals_out {\n    std::fs::write(out, evallerina::routing::to_jsonl(&proposals))\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot write proposals to {out}: {e}\"))?;\n}\n```\n\nAnd add \"proposals\" to output JSON: proposals array of to_json.\n\nWait — scenario_tool_of closure type: propose takes &dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<String>. `|_: &str| None` needs type annotation: `let no_recorded_tool = |_: &str| -> Option<String> { None };` then `&no_recorded_tool`.\n\nHmm — wait, is it right for doc-audit to ALWAYS run routing? tier0 runs doc-audit > /dev/null; routing.toml is checked in → fine. propose errors loudly if registry empty — registry is const. OK.\n\nAlso update Command::DocAudit match arm: `Command::DocAudit { proposals_out, file } => match run_doc_audit(proposals_out.as_deref(), file)`.\n\n3. Also update main.rs doc comment for DocAudit subcommand and run_doc_audit doc 